  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "ow-run",
      "title": "The OW /5 run",
      "body": "One World Under Doom is a 20-card insert in 2026 Topps Chrome Marvel Comics. The Red Refractor /5s on this list — OW-01, OW-05, OW-10, OW-15, OW-20 — all publish 1:14,712 Hobby. OW-01 starts the run; that does not make it a harder pull than OW-20. The #10–#6 order is editorial sampling of that 20-card family."
    },
    {
      "id": "solo-vs-multi",
      "title": "Solo vs Multi",
      "body": "Two of the four steepest published /5s are multi-character facsimile cards (MFQ-DNSG quad, FD-DS dual). FY-05 is the hardest solo Doctor Doom /5 on this list at 1:60,774 Value. Multi-character cards can carry steeper family odds than a solo insert with the same /5 stamp."
    },
    {
      "id": "five-not-equal",
      "title": "Why /5 ≠ equal difficulty",
      "body": "Every card here is serial /5 with a stated pop of 5. Published pack odds still range from 1:132,404 Hobby down through 1:14,712 Hobby — and easier still on the honorable mentions. Same serial is not the same pull."
    },
    {
      "id": "market-not-difficulty",
      "title": "Market ≠ difficulty",
      "body": "Sold comps and asking prices measure demand, not pack difficulty. A cheaper /5 can still be harder to rip. This ranking uses published odds, not comps."
    },
    {
      "id": "methodology",
      "title": "Methodology",
      "body": "Rank by published pack odds. Keep Hobby and Value labels as printed. When odds tie at 1:14,712 Hobby, order is editorial (OW run sampling + TB-12 as the transition into that band). Census: 61 /5 issues, 305 physical. Exclude Doom 2099, Doomasaur, Victorious, and Victor Timely. Independent NLF write-up — not official Topps or Marvel."
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Are all Doctor Doom /5 cards equally hard to pull?",
      "a": "No. Only five copies exist of each issue, but published pack odds vary by set and insert family."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why are #10–#5 in that order if they share 1:14,712 Hobby?",
      "a": "That band is tied. The order is editorial. OW-01 starts the 20-card OW run; it is not harder than OW-20. TB-12 is the editorial transition."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why is MFQ-DNSG #1?",
      "a": "It has the steepest published figure on this list: 1:132,404 Hobby."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why is FY-05 the hardest solo?",
      "a": "It publishes 1:60,774 Value — the next-steepest printed figure after the quad, and the steepest solo /5 here."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is this the same as the /24 & /25 countdown?",
